{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"The fused matrix projection is numerically unsuitable: even an unfused Triton dot uses a different float32 accumulation tree than the native projection. I’m keeping native GEMM. One safer avenue remains: normalize the tiny `B×512` response tensor once, then let the affine kernel reuse it, replacing millions of redundant divisions while preserving the exact projection. I’m checking whether Triton’s 512-way reduction matches PyTorch bit-for-bit."}}
